# Treat a non-student address as a BI student email so the BI link flow can be
# tested without a live @bi.no student mailbox. Comma-separate to map more than
# one address. The right-hand side must still be a valid s<digits> student id.
# When it fires, the Azure Graph lookup runs against the left-hand address
# (the account that still resolves in BI's tenant), so bi_employee_id and
# bi_campus_id come from that record rather than the retired student one.
#
# WARNING: this variable is the ONLY gate — there is no NODE_ENV check, because
# account linking cannot be exercised from localhost and so can only be tested
# against a real deployment. While set, the named address can assert the mapped
# student number and that student's membership. Unset it as soon as a test run
# is finished; every match logs at error level so a forgotten value is loud.
# BI_DEV_STUDENT_EMAIL_OVERRIDE="firstname.lastname@bi.no=s1715738"
BI_DEV_STUDENT_EMAIL_OVERRIDE=""

# Shows the client-side Appwrite session probe above the "Link BI Student
# Email" button. On by default outside production; set to "true" to also show
# it in a deployed environment while debugging the link flow.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BI_LINK_DEBUG=""
